// @run
// @log 7
// @log 7
// @log 7
// GRADUATED from `@no-instantiate` (silent-class-inventory D139, 2026-08-27). This file was
// the check-clean-invalid-wasm SPECIMEN — `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts`'s
// `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` — and program 1 below is that constant verbatim. It printed
// `type mismatch: expected (ref $type), found (ref $type)` out of a `vl check` that exited 0
// with no diagnostics at all. It runs.
//
// WHAT WAS WRONG WAS NOT THE MINT, AND THE PROBE IS WHAT SAID SO. The filed diagnosis was
// that two mv slots hold two genuinely different heaps — `uVarHeap[Circle]` for the arm and
// `sHeapIdx[Dot]` for the render — and that is TRUE and MUST STAY TRUE: `DECISIONS.md` keeps
// the variant and struct tables in two namespaces on purpose, and `rlSlotsLayoutTwin`
// correctly declines to merge them. Dumped on `54780e0b`, program 1 and its function-scope
// sibling intern the SAME two slots over the SAME two ref-list rows and emit BYTE-IDENTICAL
// type sections:
//
//   mv slot=0 name=Circle   kind=1 rl=0 rlnm=Circle rlheap=1 rlwrap=9   mapTy=15
//   mv slot=1 name={r:i32}  kind=1 rl=1 rlnm=Dot    rlheap=0 rlwrap=11  mapTy=16
//
// The ONLY difference is which of the two the BINDING's `Map()` resolves — `struct.new 15`
// at function scope, `struct.new 16` at module scope — and one column explains it:
//
//   function scope:  letMapShapeOf ix=18 fn=30 letType=37 ({[string]:Circle})  -> shape 0
//   module   scope:  letMapShapeOf ix=18 fn=-1 letType=-1                      -> shape 1
//
// AT FUNCTION SCOPE THE CONTEXT WAS ALREADY BEING CARRIED, BY A CARRIER THAT NEVER RAN OVER
// THE MODULE. D81's `synthDstPinAnns` pins an un-annotated `Map()` local from the annotation
// of every destination it is delivered to — `thru(x: {[string]: Circle})` is one — and it
// walked `fnStmts` only. A module-scope binding has no `fnStmts` row and never reaches
// `collectLocals` either, which is the same structural gap `synthGlobalEmptyListAnns` exists
// to close one family over. The fix is that pass's module run, with the PROGRAM node as the
// scope identifiers resolve in; the destination scan, the disagreement gate and the four
// legs are shared rather than copied.
//
// SO IT WAS D39'S CHANNEL PROBLEM AS FILED — an anonymous `{ r: 7 }` with two nominal
// claimants that only the CONTEXT separates — but NOT a missing channel. The channel was
// written, and the row's own guess that the fix would be "a third member of the
// `synthRetPinAnn` / `synthEmptyListAnn` family" is refuted: the third member is
// `synthDstPinAnn`, it already handles a bare `Map()` initializer and an arm-valued map
// annotation, and what it was missing was a caller.
//
// THE CLASS IS NOT EMPTY AND THIS FILE IS NOT THE PROOF OF ANYTHING BROADER. The successor
// specimen is `xfail-miscompile-arm-valued-map-from-a-call-result.vl` beside it — the same
// program with the map returned from a call — and D156 / D157 / D158 carry three more live
// shapes with runnable witnesses.

// 1 — the former specimen, verbatim: the map bound at MODULE scope and handed to a callee
// whose parameter names the arm. The value is never read back, which is the whole point of
// keeping it unchanged: the mismatch was at the `Map()` construction, not at a read.
type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq
type Dot = { r: i32 }
function thru(x: {[string]: Circle}) { return x }
const c = Map()
c["o"] = { r: 7 }
thru(c)
print(7)

// 2 — the same binding with the value READ BACK through the map, so the pin covers the round
// trip and not only the construction. `thru`'s result is the pinned map.
const c2 = Map()
c2["o"] = { r: 7 }
print((thru(c2)["o"] ?? { r: 0 }).r)

// 3 — the FUNCTION-scope sibling, which ran before this change and must keep running: the
// module run must not disturb the walk it was added beside.
function mk(n: i32) {
  const c3 = Map()
  c3["o"] = { r: n }
  return thru(c3)
}
print((mk(7)["o"] ?? { r: 0 }).r)
